# Lint Discipline

Agents must NEVER disable or suppress any linting check. This includes but is not
limited to:

- `eslint-disable` / `eslint-disable-next-line` comments
- `stylelint-disable` / `stylelint-disable-next-line` comments
- `prettier-ignore` comments
- `markdownlint-disable` comments
- `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` directives (unless accompanied by
  a documented rationale approved by a human)
- Any other comment or directive whose sole purpose is to silence a linter
  or type-checker warning or error

When a lint rule fires, agents must resolve the root cause by changing the code
to satisfy the rule. Only humans may decide that a rule is invalid, overly broad,
or should be suppressed.